# Hoisting moved to pnpm-workspace.yaml.
#
# pnpm 11 no longer reads public-hoist-pattern from .npmrc. It does not warn --
# the setting is simply ignored, and the root node_modules comes out empty --
# so the pattern and the reasoning behind it now live in pnpm-workspace.yaml
# under `publicHoistPattern`, which is the only place pnpm 11 reads it from.

# Resolve every package through the 1ES public read-through proxy rather than
# npmjs directly. Without this line the workspace only used the proxy on
# machines that happen to set it in ~/.npmrc -- CI and a fresh clone went
# straight to registry.npmjs.org, so "works here" and "works there" were
# fetching from different hosts.
#
# The feed is public: it needs no _authToken, which is why the URL can live in
# the repo. It is a pass-through, not a mirror with its own builds -- the
# tarballs are byte-identical to npmjs, so pnpm-lock.yaml's existing integrity
# hashes still validate and no lockfile churn comes with this change. Verified
# against turbo@2.10.9: the proxy's tarball hashes to the sha512 already
# recorded in the lockfile.
#
# This is an install-time setting only. It does not redirect publishes -- those
# are scoped to GitHub Packages by `publishConfig.registry` in
# maximal-core/maximal-electron and by the `@stuffbucket:registry=` line the
# release workflows write, and a scoped registry wins over this global one.
registry=https://packagefeedproxy.microsoft.io/npm/

# Exempt typescript from the total hoist: packages/maximal/client pins ^7.0.2
# (the native port) while every other package pins ^5.9.3. Hoisting one of them
# to the root makes it shadow the other for any dependency that resolves by
# walking up rather than through its own peer link -- which is exactly how
# eslint-plugin-perfectionist ends up calling a TS 5 API on the TS 7 module and
# dying with `isExternalModuleNameRelative is not a function`.
